[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-104321"] :question/problem "$$\nf(y,z)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,y,\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(y,z)$ above parametrizes the elliptic paraboloid defined in Cartesian coordinates as $5x=10{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Solving our equation for $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n5x=10{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2},\\,y,\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $2{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{5}{z}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection/5dcd5ba06b1f77424c1072fcbb3d833b1f8d162bfaff9cb0aae93e6cca28c62d" :answer/id #uuid "fc16b1c6-aef2-5184-9819-e8715314bf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection/789f4a6986e24d0a8b6da690621b0b2138b6273ca57fb9642e2ace6ee5080e6c" :answer/id #uuid "6e1dc630-c3fe-54a6-a22f-0f0d57e1aad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection/64b50dc7c1dcd7e3ed5e534f52654e6d2fb953f6003d6d7c50b5e8bfc0688e01" :answer/id #uuid "d8a81934-cd7f-52eb-a556-f8e04ef27728" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection/2c5f7d68bf3fd8123bdcc9d869fb5718d6d1e9764a127a28b0451b1c1d5fa7dd" :answer/id #uuid "53dc3b84-68e3-53f9-b31d-8be0839e1a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection/c3e37318da9c5f3c910cf0c746cb7e54be253fb2752b7973187c2081d014085c" :answer/id #uuid "1e623f68-b9f4-5534-a81c-e43e69b4c47f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9ee65f-e8a3-5caf-9a58-c31be02b006f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164465/selection/c3e37318da9c5f3c910cf0c746cb7e54be253fb2752b7973187c2081d014085c" :answer-field/choices ["q-164465/selection/5dcd5ba06b1f77424c1072fcbb3d833b1f8d162bfaff9cb0aae93e6cca28c62d" "q-164465/selection/789f4a6986e24d0a8b6da690621b0b2138b6273ca57fb9642e2ace6ee5080e6c" "q-164465/selection/64b50dc7c1dcd7e3ed5e534f52654e6d2fb953f6003d6d7c50b5e8bfc0688e01" "q-164465/selection/2c5f7d68bf3fd8123bdcc9d869fb5718d6d1e9764a127a28b0451b1c1d5fa7dd" "q-164465/selection/c3e37318da9c5f3c910cf0c746cb7e54be253fb2752b7973187c2081d014085c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164465" :question/id #uuid "1ac591ac-50de-5acc-afeb-b5b2a30bc572" :question/math-academy-id "q-164465" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,z)=⟨x,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,z)$ above parametrizes the hyperbolic paraboloid defined in Cartesian coordinates as $3y={z}^{2}-9{x}^{2}.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Solving our equation for $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n3y={z}^{2}-9{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,z) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2},\\,z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-3{x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164465/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "140679a6-6a14-5f92-9a92-68917f197863"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164463/selecti