"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164463" :question/id #uuid "3312d10b-5f81-5bae-a433-29944a392e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-164463" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,y)$ above parametrizes the elliptic paraboloid defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{z}{2}=3{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}.$ What is the third component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "Solving our equation for $z,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{z}{2}=3{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,z=6{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,6{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $6{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "140679a6-6a14-5f92-9a92-68917f197863"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164469/selection/52a63be074c9694e6b78e55e339f376b843a2bf091323c05ebdd6b1380a05673" :answer/id #uuid "5cdff4da-a249-5e4f-8443-a97bab00afbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164469/selection/fb69cb740e0c2d051d68009177f749097d8908de53ed6ff1b241f2b41102e702" :answer/id #uuid "91d6346c-060b-5726-9e89-8a26fe3b2651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164469/selection/c5818e94989cdad98def4c60b9259aac719335b94fcf6428e7663b8058a83674" :answer/id #uuid "8e4acb40-e3c5-5807-8d9b-9230d733443c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164469/selection/90c84fbd56d336a1a74a30adba7f2ffb388b6408cea89b0fe1334c7f592278c0" :answer/id #uuid "92aaa2ee-1bbb-5125